  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879718",
      "title": "Passing Data to Mutations with Payloads",
      "lectureOrder": 217,
      "videoOrder": 190,
      "sourceHash": "575db8f5a056af2b56d7479ffb2dc9d41a378fcef664b057f4fcd5a6f917a6ed",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.24,
          "end": 6.61,
          "en": "Now some mutations might require arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.61,
          "end": 8.69,
          "en": "Here, we got the increment mutation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.69,
          "end": 11.41,
          "en": "and the value by which we increment this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.41,
          "end": 13.853,
          "en": "is hard coded into this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15,
          "end": 17.99,
          "en": "We could add and increase mutation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.99,
          "end": 20.9,
          "en": "which also gets to state and say that in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.9,
          "end": 23.36,
          "en": "we also want to change the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.36,
          "end": 27.33,
          "en": "but we actually want to increase it by a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 31.313,
          "en": "which can be defined when this mutation is committed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.52,
          "end": 35.94,
          "en": "And you also allow for this scenario,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.94,
          "end": 39.98,
          "en": "your mutations actually also take a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.98,
          "end": 43.603,
          "en": "a payload, so a data package that can be a pendant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.62,
          "end": 47.27,
          "en": "And I'm going to name the argument payload here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.27,
          "end": 50.65,
          "en": "though of course, these names are up to you ultimately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.65,
          "end": 52.7,
          "en": "Now payload can be anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.7,
          "end": 56.42,
          "en": "It can be a number, it can be a string, it can be an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.42,
          "end": 59.78,
          "en": "And let's say here, we assume it will be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.78,
          "end": 61.723,
          "en": "where we have a value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.56,
          "end": 64.45,
          "en": "But this is entirely up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.45,
          "end": 66.73,
          "en": "it's your store, your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.73,
          "end": 70.943,
          "en": "you can expect any kind of data on committed mutations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.89,
          "end": 73.743,
          "en": "But how could we now call this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.82,
          "end": 79.37,
          "en": "Well let's and ChangeCounter, we say add two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.37,
          "end": 82.53,
          "en": "because that's more appropriate to what happens here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.53,
          "end": 85.87,
          "en": "but in App.vue, I don't want to commit increment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.87,
          "end": 88.05,
          "en": "but the new increase mutation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.18,
          "end": 91.563,
          "en": "and I want to increase TheCounter by 10.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.50999999999999,
          "end": 96.24000000000001,
          "en": "Now, I still don't want to manipulate the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.24000000000001,
          "end": 98.32,
          "en": "from insight this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.32,
          "end": 100.78,
          "en": "I still want to use a mutation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.78,
          "end": 103.86,
          "en": "but I want to pass this data package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.86,
          "end": 108.64,
          "en": "to this mutation so that we have some flexibility.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.64,
          "end": 111.72,
          "en": "For that commit, takes a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.72,
          "end": 113.46000000000001,
          "en": "which will be the payload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.46000000000001,
          "end": 116.92,
          "en": "which then later is received in your mutation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.92,
          "end": 118.39,
          "en": "So the second argument here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.39,
          "end": 122.36,
          "en": "indeed is also the second argument you can pass to commit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.36,
          "end": 124.43,
          "en": "And this can be anything as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.43,
          "end": 128.18,
          "en": "a number, a string, but here it should be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.18,
          "end": 130.7,
          "en": "with a value property because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.7,
          "end": 132.31,
          "en": "that is what I'm expecting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.31,
          "end": 136.803,
          "en": "I'm accessing dot value on the payload in my mutation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.84,
          "end": 140.39,
          "en": "So here I provide a value and in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.39,
          "end": 143.523,
          "en": "let's say the value is a number and it's the number 10.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.8,
          "end": 149.8,
          "en": "If we now save this and reload, add two adds two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.07,
          "end": 153.73,
          "en": "because it commits the increment mutation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.73,
          "end": 158.29,
          "en": "But add 10 adds 10 because it calls to increase mutation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.29,
          "end": 161.543,
          "en": "with a payload that contains this value of 10.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.11,
          "end": 168.11,
          "en": "So payloads extra data can be passed to your mutations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.32,
          "end": 172.67000000000002,
          "en": "You also got an alternative way of committing by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 172.67000000000002,
          "end": 174.71,
          "en": "there is nothing wrong with this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.71,
          "end": 179.71,
          "en": "but you can also call commit and pass an object to commit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.68,
          "end": 184.08,
          "en": "Now this object now needs to have a type property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.08,
          "end": 186.2,
          "en": "which holds the name of the mutation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 186.2,
          "end": 188.22,
          "en": "that should be committed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.22,
          "end": 192.38,
          "en": "But in addition, it can hold as many properties as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.38,
          "end": 195.35,
          "en": "For example here, this value property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 195.35,
          "end": 199.53,
          "en": "and then it's this object without the type so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.53,
          "end": 203.513,
          "en": "which will be provided as a payload to this mutation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.48,
          "end": 207.02,
          "en": "So that's simply an alternative way of committing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.02,
          "end": 209.713,
          "en": "and it's up to you, which approach you prefer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.66,
          "end": 213.363,
          "en": "This will also work as you see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.7,
          "end": 218.47,
          "en": "Now these are mutations, and the clear advantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.47,
          "end": 220.51,
          "en": "that you move the concrete logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 220.51,
          "end": 224.13,
          "en": "that changes your state into your store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 224.13,
          "end": 226.38,
          "en": "And here of course, it's very simple logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 226.38,
          "end": 229.32999999999998,
          "en": "but this could be way more complex in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 229.32999999999998,
          "end": 233.28,
          "en": "And you just commit mutations from inside your components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 233.28,
          "end": 235.7,
          "en": "so you never, and that's really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.7,
          "end": 239.93,
          "en": "You never directly add the state from inside components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 239.93,
          "end": 242.55,
          "en": "This is not considered a good practice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 242.55,
          "end": 245.313,
          "en": "You should instead use mutations.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
